    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with a lineup heavily incentivized by stolen base upside and favorable platoon dynamics. **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (78.29) stands out as our premier start; his combination of a leadoff spot, a 14% dynamic platoon boost against a right-handed pitcher, and a 100% stolen base probability projection against an exploitable battery makes him an elite play. Joining him at the top of the board is **Yordan Alvarez** (72.69), who, despite a slight park penalty, maintains high-end efficiency due to an elite xwOBA of 0.475, and **Colt Keith** (69.64), who benefits significantly from facing an inefficient arm in Rodriguez. **Trea Turner** (69.07) and **Kyle Schwarber** (67.33) round out our most potent offensive threats, both bolstered by wind-out conditions and advantageous batting order positioning, effectively mitigating the risks posed by Manaea.\n\nOur bench strategy remains disciplined, with **Casey Schmitt** (47.68) serving as the closest cut from the starting nine. While **Casey Schmitt** offered a solid platoon advantage, his efficiency projections were ultimately cannibalized by the higher categorical contributions expected from the active infielders. Meanwhile, **Carson Benge** (37.58) and **Jacob Gonzalez** (35.57) failed to clear the 40-point efficiency floor, leading to their exclusion to preserve our limited game caps. Managers should remain alert to the risk of **Dillon Dingler** (52.54), whose score is suppressed by a negative platoon shift despite a favorable matchup; however, he remains in the lineup due to his steady contribution profile. We are currently navigating a high-volatility environment with several starters facing pitchers with xERAs above 4.50, suggesting that today\u2019s aggressive deployment is well-positioned to capitalize on these defensive vulnerabilities.",
